Subject: [PATCH] mtk: cpuidle: update the owner of the prediction timer

A prediction timer belongs to a specific governor instance. Selecting
the instance with this_cpu_ptr() instead of the timer pointer can update
another CPU's history if a pending timer migrates during CPU offlining.

Derive the owner from the timer. This preserves normal pinned callbacks,
prediction thresholds, latency QoS, firmware idle states and IPI handling.
This targets the MHSP vendor module, not the common kernel boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@
 static enum hrtimer_restart histtimer_fn(struct hrtimer *h)
 {
-	struct gov_info *gov = this_cpu_ptr(&gov_infos);
+	struct gov_info *gov = container_of(h, struct gov_info, shallow.histtimer);
 
 	if (gov->shallow.timer_need_cancel)
 		gov->shallow.timer_need_cancel = false;
 	else
